  "contracts": {
    "frameStorage": "Getter returns the stored twelve-double frame. Setter copies it exactly without normalization; selected callers explicitly copy owner frame into child before insertion.",
    "ownerInsertion": "Reject null or invalid child before list insertion. For a circle, require positive stored radius, nonnull backend, nonzero backend kind and nonempty backend record range. After insertion, register child backend with owner backend. No complete transaction rollback established.",
    "placedCircle": "Transform existing local defining points forward and compare to supplied first three records. With count >=4 and all three squared distances strictly below 1e-5, inverse-transform fourth record, translate defining points and center by the resulting local center delta, refresh records and rebuild backend. Otherwise inverse-transform the supplied first three records and call three-point builder with supplied frame.",
    "inversePlacement": "Subtract translation, then multiply by transposed rotation. This is the native rigid-frame assumption, not a general affine inverse. Preserve per-component operation order.",
    "provenance": "Retained pick acquisition and exact source owner binding still need tracing; these helper contracts cannot assign a frame to otherwise unidentified data."
  },
